{"uid":"tools/sign_elf.py","name":"sign_elf.py","qualname":"tools/sign_elf.py","kind":"module","file":"tools/sign_elf.py","line":1,"end_line":497,"language":"py","signature":"","params":[],"returns":"","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"Sign MiniOS user binaries with Ed25519 (development key). .","description":"Usage: python3 tools/sign_elf.py [--check] [--key-id N] FILE [FILE ...] python3 tools/sign_elf.py [--check] [--key-id N] --walk DIR [DIR ...] . Inputs: ET_EXEC/ET_DYN ELF files. Other files are skipped, never modified. Outputs: the same files with a signature note carrying one key id byte plus the 64-byte signature, either patched into an existing PT_NOTE/SHT_NOTE slot or appended as a new non-allocated .note.minios.sign section. With --check nothing is written; unsigned or badly signed images are reported and the exit status is 1. . Failure modes: non-ELF input skips silently; truncated headers, missing section tables on images without a note slot, and unknown key ids fail loudly with a non-zero exit. Signing is idempotent: an image whose current bytes already verify under the requested key is left untouched, so rebuilds stay mtime-stable. . The development seed below is a published test key for dogfood builds only (docs/spec/kernel.md). Production images use key id 1 with a key file passed through MINIOS_SIGN_KEY.","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"","members":["tools/sign_elf.py::Config","tools/sign_elf.py::sha512","tools/sign_elf.py::encodepoint_raw","tools/sign_elf.py::edwards_add","tools/sign_elf.py::scalarmult","tools/sign_elf.py::base_point","tools/sign_elf.py::publickey","tools/sign_elf.py::sign_digest","tools/sign_elf.py::pad_to","tools/sign_elf.py::parse_ehdr","tools/sign_elf.py::parse_phdrs","tools/sign_elf.py::canonical_digest","tools/sign_elf.py::find_note_slots","tools/sig